<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Architectural Framework | Ashley Keller</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
    <style>
        /* Additional styling specific to pillars page */
        .pillar-icon {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            color: #00a1e0;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }
        .pillar-card {
            border-left: 4px solid;
            transition: transform 0.3s ease;
        }
        .pillar-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
        }
        .pillar-1 { border-left-color: #00a1e0; }
        .pillar-2 { border-left-color: #4bca81; }
        .pillar-3 { border-left-color: #ff9a3c; }
        .methodology-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding-left: 0;
        }
        .methodology-list li {
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            padding-left: 1.5rem;
            position: relative;
        }
        .methodology-list li:before {
            content: "✓";
            color: #00a1e0;
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <!-- Navigation (same as your main site) -->
    <header>
        <div class="container header-container">
            <div class="logo"><a href="../index.html">Ashley<span>Keller</span></a></div>
            <!-- Include your mobile menu here -->
        </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <section class="container" style="padding-top: 3rem;">
        <h1>Architectural Framework</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Building scalable, secure foundations that enable business growth without introducing technical debt</p>
        
        <div class="intro-box">
            <p>My approach is guided by core principles focused on creating maintainable systems that scale with business needs. Each pillar represents a fundamental aspect of sustainable Salesforce architecture.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillars Grid -->
        <div class="pillars-grid" style="display: grid; gap: 2rem; margin: 3rem 0;">
            
            <!-- Pillar 1 -->
            <div class="pillar-card pillar-1" style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
                <div class="pillar-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-layer-group"></i>
                </div>
                <h2>Pillar 1: Foundational Scalability & Maintainability</h2>
                <p><strong>Core Principle:</strong> Build systems that grow efficiently with the business while remaining easy to maintain.</p>
                
                <h3>Methodology</h3>
                <ul class="methodology-list">
                    <li><strong>Declarative-First Approach:</strong> Implementing process automation with Flow before considering custom code</li>
                    <li><strong>Modular Design:</strong> Creating reusable, independent components (Aura actions, subflows, LWC)</li>
                    <li><strong>Scalable Data Modeling:</strong> Focus on simplicity, avoiding unnecessary relationships</li>
                    <li><strong>Schema Simplicity:</strong> Maintaining reporting and system performance as data grows</li>
                </ul>
                
                <div class="in-practice" style="background: #f3f6f9; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 5px; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <h4><i class="fas fa-rocket"></i> In Practice</h4>
                    <p>See this pillar applied in my <a href="../index.html#case-study">Greenfield Implementation Case Study</a>, particularly in the data model design and automation architecture.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Pillar 2 -->
            <div class="pillar-card pillar-2" style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
                <div class="pillar-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-database"></i>
                </div>
                <h2>Pillar 2: Data Integrity & Cleanliness</h2>
                <p><strong>Core Principle:</strong> Data is a core company asset - "garbage in, garbage out" is not an option.</p>
                
                <h3>Methodology</h3>
                <ul class="methodology-list">
                    <li><strong>Proactive Governance:</strong> Validation of data input via API or manual entry</li>
                    <li><strong>Correct Data Typing:</strong> Choosing appropriate field types to ensure accuracy</li>
                    <li><strong>Systematic Hygiene:</strong> Proactive monitoring using Salesforce Health Check</li>
                    <li><strong>Standardization:</strong> Using standard objects and features when possible to reduce complexity</li>
                </ul>
                
                <div class="in-practice" style="background: #f3f6f9; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 5px; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <h4><i class="fas fa-rocket"></i> In Practice</h4>
                    <p>Explore the <a href="#">Data Governance Framework</a> I implemented for a financial services client, reducing data errors by 85%.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Pillar 3 -->
            <div class="pillar-card pillar-3" style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
                <div class="pillar-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i>
                </div>
                <h2>Pillar 3: Security & Compliance by Design</h2>
                <p><strong>Core Principle:</strong> Principle of Least Privilege as the cornerstone of security models.</p>
                
                <h3>Methodology</h3>
                <ul class="methodology-list">
                    <li><strong>Modern Permission Set Approach:</strong> Implementing granular, audit-ready access controls</li>
                    <li><strong>Logical Visibility Models:</strong> Role hierarchy and sharing rules that protect sensitive data</li>
                    <li><strong>Secure Collaboration:</strong> Balancing data protection with necessary team access</li>
                    <li><strong>Compliance Integration:</strong> Building regulatory requirements into the foundation</li>
                </ul>
                
                <div class="in-practice" style="background: #f3f6f9; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 5px; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <h4><i class="fas fa-rocket"></i> In Practice</h4>
                    <p>Review the <a href="#">Security Model Summary</a> for a healthcare implementation that achieved HIPAA compliance through designed-in security controls.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Integration Section -->
        <div class="integration" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #032d60 0%, #00a1e0 100%); color: white; padding: 2.5rem; border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="color: white;">How These Pillars Work Together</h2>
            <p>These pillars are not independent concepts but interconnected principles that reinforce each other:</p>
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: white;">Scalable Foundation</h3>
                    <p>Enables clean data practices and secure access models to function efficiently at any scale.</p>
                </div>
                <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: white;">Clean Data</h3>
                    <p>Supports accurate reporting and analytics while reducing security risks from inaccurate information.</p>
                </div>
                <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: white;">Designed Security</h3>
                    <p>Protects the scalable infrastructure and valuable data assets from inception through growth.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Call to Action -->
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem; padding: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid #eee;">
            <h3>See This Framework in Action</h3>
            <p>Explore how I apply these principles in real-world implementations:</p>
            <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; margin-top: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                <a href="../index.html#case-study" class="btn">View Case Study</a>
                <a href="../index.html#projects" class="btn btn-outline" style="border-color: white; color: white; background: transparent;">Other Projects</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer (same as your main site) -->
    <footer>
        <!-- Your existing footer -->
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
